      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa has a yield strength of about 800 MPa at lower temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa sustains roughly 40% strain under lower-temperature testing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped TiVNbTa has a yield strength of about 330 MPa at 1273 K.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped TiVNbTa has a compressive strength of 423 MPa at 30% strain and 1273 K.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 2 at.% Hf should be added to TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed alloy is to be vacuum arc melted, homogenized at approximately 1473 K, and aged at approximately 1073 K.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed heat treatment will promote precipitate formation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minor Hf alloying can form nanoscopic precipitates that remain stable in the BCC TiVNbTa matrix at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-based precipitates will pin dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-based precipitates will strengthen grain boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitate strengthening can reduce high-temperature softening by retaining microstructural stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, Hf-doped TiVNbTa will have a yield strength 15–30% above the approximately 330 MPa undoped baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-doped TiVNbTa will retain ductility comparable to that of undoped TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention applies to mechanical testing from room temperature through 1273 K under loads representative of W/CuCrZr intermediate-layer service.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The expected performance benefit occurs chiefly below approximately 1300 K.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Hf additions may produce brittle intermetallic phases.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The exact optimum Hf concentration and precipitate fraction in TiVNbTa are not established experimentally.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
